      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database remains inaccessible (persistent authentication error `1045 Access denied`), so live verification isn't possible. I'll finalize based on the strong semantic-network evidence and the provided gold-table/join-key hints, which exactly match the entities I investigated.\n\n---\n\n## Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (gold set):**\n- **FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY** — Bridge table: one row per organization–DLC key assignment. Columns: `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` (FK to FCLT_ORGANIZATION), `DLC_KEY`. Used to filter organizations that have a DLC key assignment before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION for DLC-level facility/room statistics.\n- **FCLT_ORGANIZATION** — Facilities organization dimension (one row per organization, levels 1–6). Key columns: `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` (joins to FCLT_ROOMS and FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY), `HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME` (\"Department name as recorded in HR systems\" — the department name for the room side), `DLC_KEY`, `ORGANIZATION_LEVEL`, `ASSIGNABLE`.\n- **FCLT_ROOMS** — Room inventory (one row per physical room). Key columns: `AREA` (\"Room area in square meters; used in area statistics (average, range, variance)\" — explicitly documented for exactly this task shape), `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` (organization assignment = \"rooms assigned to department\").\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Catalog-level subject offering per term/academic year. Key columns: `TOTAL_UNITS` (\"Total credit units of the subject\"), `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (\"Offering department name, e.g. 'Mathematics'\"), `TERM_CODE` (joins to term tables).\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — Term dimension. Key columns: `TERM_CODE`, `IS_REGULAR_TERM` (\"'Y'/'N' flag indicating a regular term (Fall/Spring)… only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS, not in ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\").\n\n**Related tables examined and set aside:** SPACE_UNIT/SPACE_DETAIL (space-unit assignment perspective, square footage, different key family), FAC_ROOMS/FAC_ORGANIZATION (FAC_* snapshot family), FCLT_ROOMS_HIST (fiscal-period history), HR_ORG_UNIT (HR attributes via DLC_KEY, fan-out risk documented), SIS_DEPARTMENT/STUDENT_DEPARTMENT (academic department lookups — not needed since both fact tables carry department names), SUBJECT_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (registrar enrollment process, not catalog offerings), ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (lacks IS_REGULAR_TERM), CIS/DRUPAL catalogs (alternative feeds).\n\n**Metrics:** dw_4061 (same-shape precedent: AVG/MAX−MIN/VARIANCE of FCLT_ROOMS.AREA with `AREA > 40`, plus total-units stats from COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED filtered `IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'`), dw_1488 (range/variance of room area precedent), dw_1833, dw_1465, dw_2559, dw_3410, dw_4776, dw_4330, dw_3235, dw_3153, dw_3332 (FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY usage precedents), dw_2151, dw_41, dw_3417, dw_2597, dw_1049 (total-units statistics precedents).\n\n**Concepts:** concept_room_space_inventory, concept_facility_organization_dimension, concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_department_dimension, concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy.\n\n**Column concepts:** column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_term_code, column_concept_facility_organization_key, column_concept_dlc_key.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- Graph edges confirm: FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY ↔ FCLT_ORGANIZATION (joins, incoming), FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY ↔ FCLT_ROOMS (joins, outgoing), FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY ↔ MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY; FCLT_ROOMS ↔ FCLT_ORGANIZATION via `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`; COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ↔ ACADEMIC_TERMS via `TERM_CODE`; COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ↔ FCLT_ROOMS via `MEET_PLACE = FCLT_ROOM_KEY` (not needed here).\n- `metrics_by_table` on FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY returned 8 metrics — all use it as the DLC-assignment filter before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION, exactly as the hint decomposition does.\n- column_concept_dlc_key membership includes FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY; column_concept_facility_organization_key documents `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` as the join key across FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (room-area source candidates):**\n\n| Dimension | FCLT_ROOMS | SPACE_DETAIL | FAC_ROOMS | FCLT_ROOMS_HIST |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per room (cited: table desc) | one row per room assigned to a space unit (cited: desc) | one row per room, FAC_* keys (cited: desc) | one row per room per fiscal period (cited: desc) |\n| Area measure | `AREA` in m², \"used in area statistics (average, range, variance)\" (cited: column def) | room square footage (cited: desc) | same structure as FCLT_ROOMS (cited: desc) | area per period (cited: desc) |\n| Org attribution | `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` direct (cited: column def) | via SPACE_UNIT bridge (cited: desc) | FAC_ORGANIZATION (cited: desc) | per-period assignment (cited: desc) |\n| Time semantics | current snapshot | current | snapshot | historical (201505) |\n\n**Total-units source candidates:** column_concept_total_units comparisons state COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS is the \"catalog-declared unit value per offering\" while SUBJECT_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY are registrar values; its decision_guide maps \"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance…) over catalog offerings\" → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS.\n\n**Term filter candidates:** ACADEMIC_TERMS carries `IS_REGULAR_TERM`; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL explicitly \"does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM\" (cited: table desc) — so \"regular academic terms\" is only supported by ACADEMIC_TERMS.\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping:**\n\n| Requirement | FCLT_ROOMS+FCLT_ORGANIZATION+FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED+ACADEMIC_TERMS |\n|---|---|---|\n| rooms assigned to department | SUPPORTED (`FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` on both; DLC bridge filter per 8 metric precedents) | n/a |\n| area > 40 filter, avg/range/variance of AREA | SUPPORTED (`AREA` column def cites these exact statistics) | n/a |\n| department name (room side) | SUPPORTED (`HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME`, per hint mapping) | n/a |\n| subjects offered in regular terms | n/a | SUPPORTED (`TERM_CODE` join + `IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'`) |\n| avg/range/variance of total units | n/a | SUPPORTED (`TOTAL_UNITS`, decision_guide precedent) |\n| SPACE_DETAIL alternative | NOT-SUPPORTED for this wording (space-unit perspective, no direct org-key room assignment; no DLC-bridge precedent) | — |\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"rooms assigned to department\" anchors to FCLT_ROOMS.`FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` = FCLT_ORGANIZATION.`FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` (column def: \"Organization key of the room\"); \"department name\" on the room side anchors to `HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME` and on the subject side to `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (both listed in the hint's column mapping); \"regular academic terms\" anchors uniquely to ACADEMIC_TERMS.`IS_REGULAR_TERM`; \"area greater than 40\" anchors to FCLT_ROOMS.`AREA > 40`. The two department-name columns live in different domains (HR vs academic) but the hint mapping explicitly lists both for \"department name\", and dw_4061 precedent shows the two fact groups are combined per department in one report.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** AREA>40 + AVG/range/VARIANCE precedents: dw_4061 (FCLT_ROOMS), dw_1488 (FCLT_ROOMS). FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY-as-filter precedents: 8 metrics (dw_1833, dw_3332, dw_3410, dw_2559, dw_3153, dw_4330, dw_3235, dw_4776). IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y' + TOTAL_UNITS statistics precedents: dw_4061, dw_41, dw_3417, dw_1049, dw_4387.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nFCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY is consistently used to restrict room/organization statistics to DLC-assigned organizations; FCLT_ROOMS serves room-size dispersion questions; COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves catalog unit-structure statistics by department/term; ACADEMIC_TERMS serves regular-term/current-term filtering. dw_4061 is the closest composite precedent (department-level unit statistics + room-area avg/range/variance with AREA > 40 in one report).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n- FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY: semantic_get, semantic_graph (neighbors, metrics_by_table) ✔\n- FCLT_ORGANIZATION: semantic_search, semantic_get, graph neighbors ✔\n- FCLT_ROOMS: semantic_get, graph neighbors (joins) ✔\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get, graph neighbors (joins) ✔\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS: semantic_get ✔\n- dw_4061, dw_1488: semantic_get (full SQL) ✔; other metrics: desc-level from search/metrics_by_table ✔\n- column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name: semantic_get (comparisons, decision_guide) ✔\n- Concepts (room_space_inventory, facility_organization_dimension, subject_offering_facts, academic_term_dimension, course_catalog_sources, department_dimension, dept_hr_org_hierarchy, dlc_key, facility_organization_key, term_code): retrieved via search descs ✔\n- mysql_query: attempted 6 times — all failed with server-side authentication error `1045 Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`; live data verification was impossible. SQL is therefore grounded in the hint decomposition (which matches the semantic evidence exactly) and metric precedents.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Room side: FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY → FCLT_ORGANIZATION (via `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`) → FCLT_ROOMS (via `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`), filter `AREA > 40`, group by `HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME`. Subject side: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED → ACADEMIC_TERMS (via `TERM_CODE`), filter `IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'`, group by `DEPARTMENT_NAME`. Combine the two per-department aggregates by joining on department name (INNER JOIN, so each output row carries all seven requested columns).\n\n**6b.** Two CTEs (one per aggregation grain) joined on department name — this avoids any fan-out between room rows and offering rows. Range = `MAX − MIN`; variance = `VARIANCE()` (population, matching dw_4061/dw_1488 precedents); no ROUND anywhere per \"Do not return any rounded answers\". SELECT list is exactly the 7 requested columns in the asked order.\n\n**6c.** Data perspective: `AREA` column def explicitly cites average/range/variance usage; `IS_REGULAR_TERM` exists only in ACADEMIC_TERMS; separate CTEs keep room-grain and offering-grain rows from multiplying each other. Semantic-network perspective: join edges FCLT_ORGANIZATION↔FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY↔FCLT_ROOMS and COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED↔ACADEMIC_TERMS are documented graph relations; column_concept_total_units decision_guide selects the catalog table for unit statistics. Business perspective: dw_4061 is a direct same-shape precedent (AREA>40 room stats + regular-term catalog unit stats per department); 8 metrics precedent the DLC-bridge filter.\n\n**6d.** Caveat: because the DB was unreachable, the join-match rate between `HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME` and `DEPARTMENT_NAME` could not be measured; the hint's column mapping explicitly lists both columns for \"department name\", which is the discriminating evidence for joining the two aggregates on name equality. If HR names didn't overlap academic names, a LEFT JOIN variant would be the alternative — but the hint mapping and dw_4061's per-department composite pattern support the name-equality join.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_c4fce861c22f4bf89164a18e",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"WITH room_stats AS (\\n    SELECT o.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME AS department_name,\\n           AVG(r.AREA) AS avg_area,\\n           MAX(r.AREA) - MIN(r.AREA) AS area_range,\\n           VARIANCE(r.AREA) AS area_variance\\n    FROM FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY d\\n    JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION o ON d.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY = o.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\\n    JOIN FCLT_ROOMS r ON o.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY = r.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\\n    WHERE r.AREA > 40\\n    GROUP BY o.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n),\\nunit_stats AS (\\n    SELECT c.DEPARTMENT_NAME AS department_name,\\n           AVG(c.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units,\\n           MAX(c.TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(c.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_range,\\n           VARIANCE(c.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance\\n    FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED c\\n    JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t ON c.TERM_CODE = t.TERM_CODE\\n    WHERE t.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'\\n    GROUP BY c.DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n)\\nSELECT rs.department_name,\\n       rs.avg_area,\\n       rs.area_range,\\n       rs.area_variance,\\n       us.avg_total_units,\\n       us.total_units_range,\\n       us.total_units_variance\\nFROM room_stats rs\\nJOIN unit_stats us ON rs.department_name = us.department_name\\nORDER BY rs.area_range DESC;\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
